WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:10.183
Jason pointed to the screen. "We're making bread today!"

2
00:00:10.184 --> 00:00:15.337
Nina yawned loudly. "Excuse me."

3
00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:21.316
Chef frowned. "Nina, are you bored with cooking?"

4
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:23.694
Nina felt embarrassed.

5
00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:29.219
"Oh, no, Chef! My little sister has an earache.

6
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.402
She woke up last night crying.

7
00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:35.218
I didn't sleep well."

8
00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.551
"I see. Well, try to stay awake today in class."

9
00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:42.957
Nina nodded.

10
00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:46.532
Chef put four large bowls on the counter.

11
00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:50.039
He gave everyone a plastic bag.

12
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.697
"Mix your dough in these bags.

13
00:00:52.698 --> 00:00:57.802
Putting the bags in a bowl makes it easier to add ingredients."

14
00:00:57.803 --> 00:01:01.520
"Poor Lulu!" Izzie whispered.

15
00:01:01.521 --> 00:01:04.356
"Earaches hurt!"

16
00:01:04.357 --> 00:01:10.252
Nina nodded. "Mom is bringing her to the doctor today."

17
00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:13.297
The kids put their bags in the bowls.

18
00:01:13.298 --> 00:01:17.442
They poured in one cup of flour and three tablespoons of sugar.

19
00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:21.021
Then they added the yeast and warm water.

20
00:01:21.022 --> 00:01:23.195
"Now seal your bags.

21
00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:27.533
Make sure all the air is out," Chef said.

22
00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:31.385
The kids sealed the bags and mixed the ingredients.

23
00:01:31.386 --> 00:01:34.270
Bobby read from the recipe.

24
00:01:34.271 --> 00:01:38.763
"Let dough sit for ten to fifteen minutes."

25
00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:44.015
His face lit up. "Let's go outside!"

26
00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:50.922
"No, we'll learn something instead," Chef said.

27
00:01:50.923 --> 00:01:56.738
"Yeast is a fungus. The warm water activates it.

28
00:01:56.739 --> 00:02:02.804
The yeast feeds off the sugar, and it starts fermenting.

29
00:02:02.805 --> 00:02:06.278
That makes the dough rise."

30
00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:13.626
Izzie made a face. "Ew! We're eating fungus!"

31
00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:20.132
"Do you eat mushrooms? They're a fungus," Jason said.

32
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.514
"That's right," Chef said.

33
00:02:23.515 --> 00:02:27.551
Soon it was time to add more ingredients.

34
00:02:27.552 --> 00:02:34.749
The kids added salt, olive oil, and another cup of flour.

35
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.236
"We mix everything together.

36
00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.184
Then we add the last cup of flour," Jason said.

37
00:02:42.185 --> 00:02:48.877
Bobby sighed. "And mix again."

38
00:02:48.878 --> 00:02:53.309
Chef laid out parchment paper and sprinkled it with flour.

39
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.776
"Put flour on your hands too.

40
00:02:55.777 --> 00:02:59.165
That way the dough won't stick to them."

41
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.553
The kids placed their dough on the paper.

42
00:03:02.554 --> 00:03:05.952
Chef set the timer for ten minutes.

43
00:03:05.953 --> 00:03:08.577
"We knead for ten minutes.

44
00:03:08.578 --> 00:03:12.896
Kneading dough makes me feel better when I'm in a bad mood."

45
00:03:12.897 --> 00:03:17.912
"I hope it works today," Bobby whispered to Jason.

46
00:03:17.913 --> 00:03:23.975
Jason laughed.

47
00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:29.181
Suddenly Nina had an idea.

48
00:03:29.182 --> 00:03:31.870
She pounded her dough.

49
00:03:31.871 --> 00:03:34.462
She folded it.

50
00:03:34.463 --> 00:03:36.464
She squeezed it.

51
00:03:36.465 --> 00:03:40.545
"Take that, you mean earache!" she thought.

52
00:03:40.546 --> 00:03:44.291
"Stop hurting Lulu!"

53
00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:47.714
The other kids got tired, but Nina didn't.

54
00:03:47.715 --> 00:03:50.163
She kept kneading.

55
00:03:50.164 --> 00:03:54.071
When the timer went off, they formed loaves with the dough.

56
00:03:54.072 --> 00:03:58.148
They covered the loaves with warm, damp towels.

57
00:03:58.149 --> 00:04:00.336
"The dough needs to rise.

58
00:04:00.337 --> 00:04:03.728
Time to clean up," Chef said.

59
00:04:03.729 --> 00:04:08.610
The kids washed dishes, wiped the counters, and swept the floor.

60
00:04:08.611 --> 00:04:13.595
"I'm going to give my loaf to Lulu," Nina said to Izzie.

61
00:04:13.596 --> 00:04:18.029
Izzie grinned. "Good idea."

62
00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.100
"Cool!" Bobby pointed to the loaves.

63
00:04:22.101 --> 00:04:25.433
"They're rising!"

64
00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:33.509
Chef nodded. "The yeast gives off carbon dioxide and makes the bread rise."

65
00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:37.703
Soon he put the loaves in the oven.

66
00:04:37.704 --> 00:04:44.716
A while later Nina's mother walked in with Lulu.

67
00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.879
"Lulu, let's go outside.

68
00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.579
I'll show you the animals!" Nina said.

69
00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.911
Lulu met the goats and chickens.

70
00:04:55.912 --> 00:05:00.468
She loved petting Cinnamon.

71
00:05:00.469 --> 00:05:07.138
When the bread was ready, they went back inside.

72
00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:12.241
"Look, Lulu! I made this bread for you!" Nina said.

73
00:05:12.242 --> 00:05:18.400
Lulu clapped. "Lulu is all better!"

